description_en:
This is an advanced course in material science designed for students in fields of materials processing and manufacturing. Fundamental material science including material structure, phase transformations, plastic deformation, defects, fracture theory and practical material analysis technology are addressed in this course, helping students to master the key elements of engineering materials in practical application and laying a solid foundation of material science for future mechanical engineers.
This course covers：
•Introduction to metal physics, including fundamental crystallography, reciprocal lattice, crystal diffraction, etc.；
•Phase diagrams analysis and principles of phase transformation based on alloy thermodynamics;
•Defects in solids, especially dislocation theory;
•Strength theories and fracture analysis (ductile fracture, brittle fracture, crack propagation, etc.);
•Practical material analysis technology.

