Objectives:
Students will be able to understand the structure characteristics and main component types of the car body, and master the basic principles of structural finite element analysis. On this basis, they will master the beam elements and shell elements commonly used in the finite element analysis of the car body structure, and apply them to the analysis of the stiffness, strength and vibration performance of the car body structure.

The contents of the course include two main lines: 1) The basic principle of Finite Element Method - The commonly used elements of car body structure-The stiffness, strength and vibration analysis of the body structure. 2) Load analysis of body structure - Bending and torsional load- Mechanics performance evaluation (bending and torsional stiffness and strength, bending and torsional vibration frequency) of the body structure. 

The details are as follows:
Chapter 1 Introduction (body design requirements; main functions, main types and main components of body structure; the purpose of body structure analysis);
Chapter 2 Preparatory Knowledge (matrix concept, basic operations, determinants, eigenvalues)
Chapter 3 Finite element analysis method of body structure (basic principle of FEM; the use of finite element software);
Chapter 4 Analysis of beam element (element stiffness matrix);
Chapter 5 Analysis of shell element (bending analysis of thin plate, element stiffness matrix);
Chapter 6 Load analysis of body structure;
Chapter 7 Analysis of stiffness and deformation of body structure (method, examples);
Chapter 8 Strength and fatigue analysis of body structure (method, examples)
Chapter 9 Basic Principles of Finite Element Dynamics Analysis (principle, examples)
Chapter 10 Vibration analysis of body structure (basic principle, examples);
Chapter 11 Optimization of body structure (method, examples)

