description_en:
This course aims to introduce the core concepts and commonly used statistical methods in biostatistics and bioinformatics, covering topics such as data types, experimental design, statistical inference, large-scale statistical inference, genetic statistics, clinical trials, survival analysis, and bioinformatics. Through this course, students will be able to:
•	Understand the core issues and data types in biostatistics and bioinformatics;
•	Master fundamental biostatistical inference methods, including analysis of variance (ANOVA), nonparametric tests, categorical data analysis, and survival analysis;
•	Learn to apply statistical methods to solve problems in medicine, biology, and public health;
•	Grasp the fundamental framework of large-scale statistical inference, including hypothesis testing, multiple comparisons, and False Discovery Rate (FDR) control;
•	Gain an understanding of the basic concepts of bioinformatics and its connection to biostatistics, such as high-throughput data analysis, genome-wide association studies (GWAS), proteomics, and transcriptomics analysis.

