description_en:
Life is multi-scale and multi-dimensional. After nearly 4 billion years of evolution, the complex system of life shows precision, order and dynamic coordination at the multi-scale level of molecule, cell, tissue and organs, which is far beyond all the man-made systems so far. The rapid  development of life science and biotechnology in recent 100 years has made it possible for human beings to understand life, regulate life and reconstruct life on all scales. In particular, the rapid development and integration of synthetic biology, cell and tissue engineering and other emerging disciplines provide rich and powerful tools for construction and manufacturing of multi-scaled artificial biological systems such as molecules, cells, tissues and organs, and provide unlimited design and imagination for bionic recreation.

The main contents of this course include:
1） As a characteristic of complex system, how to produce molecules, cells, tissues and organs and build order;
2） Basic principles of multi-scale life system manufacturing;
3） Manufacturing principle of biological macromolecules:
4） Principle of artificial cell manufacturing
5） Principles of artificial tissue manufacturing
6） Manufacturing principle of artificial organs;
7） Application of biological system manufacturing in modern medicine

