This course is an integrated course in economics. It aims to integrate the basic knowledge and leading-edge content of modern economics by guiding students to learn Chinese economic thoughts and practices. On the one hand, this course uses the Chinese economy as a laboratory to give students an intuitive feeling of economic activities. This is the basic of economics and other social science learning, similar to the experimental classes of natural science learning. On the other hand, through understanding the Chinese economy, inspire the understanding of economics, and truly start to learn economics fully, systematically understand the basic knowledge and leading-edge content of modern economics. This course begins with “The whole picture of China’s economy history: the differences between Chinese and Western economic thoughts and practices”, carries out discussion from “farmers, agriculture and government”, “civil enterprises, state-owned enterprises, industries” “money, finance, realty” "consumption, investment, macroeconomic fluctuations" "public finance and state behavior" "China and the World" and other perspectives, and finally makes "long-term development prospects."
